<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    RUT_Umbra — RESTORED 2026-09-21 (UMBRA_IS_A_REGION_NOT_A_BIOME_1 addendum, FOUNDRY)
    as a live-continuity duplicate of `RUT_FuelSnows`, NOT a revert of the rename.

    Why: `UMBRA_IS_A_REGION_NOT_A_BIOME_1` deleted this file outright and redeployed
    with the pruning apply flag, on the recorded (but unverified) claim that 2,531
    world tiles on the canonical save carried this defName. That claim was CHECKED against the live
    canonical save, offline, via `worldmap.py`'s WorldGrid decoder (biome shortHash
    15270, resolved from a def-dump capture taken 2026-09-21T08:56:31Z, before the
    rename deploy) against `CANONICAL_ASHKARR_START_2026-09-12.rws` —
    **CONFIRMED: exactly 2,531 tiles carry this shortHash**, and the live deployed
    Mods folder (checked directly) no longer defines it anywhere — so those tiles'
    biome was genuinely UNRESOLVABLE on the next load, not a stale/pre-ruling number.

    This file exists ONLY so that defName resolves again for those tiles until the
    terminal repaint (`BIOME_PAINT_ONCE_AT_THE_END_1`) reassigns them to
    `RUT_FuelSnows`. It is a full behavioural duplicate of `RUT_FuelSnows.xml` — same
    terrain/weather/fauna/flora, nothing re-authored — so any tile still carrying the
    old name plays exactly as it did before the rename. `RUT_FuelSnows` remains the
    real, forward-authored def; new content and any future biome-mapping work should
    target it, not this file. Retire this file again once the terminal repaint has
    moved every `RUT_Umbra`-tagged tile onto `RUT_FuelSnows` (verify with the same
    `worldmap.py` check before deleting).

    Original 2026-09-09 authoring header (BIOME_OWNERSHIP_WAVE_1), preserved verbatim
    below for provenance:

    RUT_Umbra                                      UtinniPatches - authored 2026-09-09
    BIOME_OWNERSHIP_WAVE_1. Full sheet: design/Jawa/worldbuilding/biomes/
    the_propane_lakes.md (FROZEN). Replaces the donor `AB_PropaneLakes` (Alpha
    Biomes) on its LAND tiles only — the lake itself is a separate, already-owned
    worldmap water biome, `RUT_PropaneLake` (57 tiles, `LIQUID_BIOMES_MAP_1`, paint
    DONE per that sheet's Owed). Named `RUT_Umbra` rather than a "PropaneLakes"
    variant to avoid colliding with that existing water-biome defName — the sheet's
    own name for the antistellar cap region IS Umbra (SS0).

    MEASURED (sheet SS0): 2,531 tiles, arc 132-179 (sun 49-76 deg below horizon),
    temp p10/median/p90 -73.0/-62.2/-47.8 C — the coldest LAND on the planet.
    Regions Deadstone/Umbra/Ammonia Flats.

    Weather: SS4b and ban 3 rule this directly — "Aurora-clear — the common state.
    No visibility blockage (owner): starlight and curtain-light; ranged fire works;
    the sky is the most beautiful on the planet." Fog/Rain/RainyThunderstorm/
    FoggyRain all zeroed (ban 3 + ban 7 no rain, R-H1); Clear made dominant.
    SnowGentle/SnowHard kept high, reflavored per the sheet as "fuel snow" (SS4b,
    hydrocarbon/ammonia precipitation feeding the crystal flora) — not literal
    water snow, same reskin-in-place pattern The Rot's sheet uses for its own
    weather. DryThunderstorm kept low ("dry lightning over a fuel field," SS4b) —
    ban 4 requires ignition to need a hot source or spark, so this stays rare, never
    dominant.

    animalDensity/plantDensity/diseaseMtbDays kept at the donor's own values (sheet
    SS0 "Donor inventory taken in" lists these as read-in, not disputed).

    wildAnimals/wildPlants: transplanted from BiomeCast_Ashkarr.xml /
    BiomeFlora_Ashkarr.xml against rosters/the_propane_lakes.json. Ban 1 (no icy
    dayside analogs) and ban 2 (no kyber) are both roster-level bans already
    enforced by that JSON's own evictions, not re-checked field-by-field here.

    NOT this pass's scope: `ANCIENT_WAR_LAB_1` (the sealed lab beneath the lake);
    the electrojet tap building; the crater-event map permanence; the island
    landmark (tile 5873); any world repaint (paint already DONE for the lake per
    the sheet's Owed — this def is the land only, un-painted).

  -->

  <BiomeDef>
    <defName>RUT_Umbra</defName>
    <label>Umbra</label>
    <description>The far end of the world: a black sea of liquid fuel under the brightest sky on the planet, ringed by frozen ammonia flats. It snows fuel. The aurora is the strongest anywhere -- the magnetosphere slamming back together after its rude shock upstream -- so the ice glows green and violet even without a moon. The fast things run in blue flame, because nothing moves fluidly here without burning; the plants are crystal, and grow overnight from what falls.</description>
    <workerClass>AlphaBiomes.BiomeWorker_PropaneLakes</workerClass>

    <!-- OWNER RULING 2026-09-19 (RUT_UMBRA_ROADS_RULING_1): the ban STANDS. No
         roads in the Umbra, same as RUT_ExtremeDesert's "No roads through the deep
         dune". This flag was previously an unexamined default with no sheet behind
         it; it is now ruled and the sheet says so.
         MEASURED (2026-09-07 link export): 42 Umbra tiles carry stored road links,
         and 74 of their 78 links run Umbra-to-Umbra - only 4 leave the region. So
         the ban costs almost no connectivity: it hides an internal web in the
         coldest land on the planet, not a route to anywhere.
         Nothing is destroyed by this. `potentialRoads` keeps every link in the
         world data (2,470 across the planet, unchanged); the flag only decides
         whether they DRAW. Flipping this to true restores all 42 tiles with no
         re-authoring, should the Assailant/Rakata-vault pilgrimage ever want a
         road in. -->
    <allowRoads>false</allowRoads>
    <allowRivers>false</allowRivers>
    <allowFarmingCamps>true</allowFarmingCamps>
    <animalDensity>0.5</animalDensity>
    <plantDensity>0.75</plantDensity>
    <forageability>0.0</forageability>
    <movementDifficulty>1.5</movementDifficulty>
    <texture>Biomes/AB_PropaneLakes</texture>
    <diseaseMtbDays>110</diseaseMtbDays>
    <diseases>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_Flu</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>100</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_Plague</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>80</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_FibrousMechanites</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>30</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_SensoryMechanites</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>30</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_AnimalFlu</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>100</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_AnimalPlague</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>80</commonality>
      </li>
    </diseases>
    <terrainsByFertility>
      <li>
        <terrain>AB_PackedSnow</terrain>
        <min>-999</min>
        <max>0.87</max>
      </li>
      <li>
        <terrain>AB_PackedIce</terrain>
        <min>0.87</min>
        <max>999</max>
      </li>
    </terrainsByFertility>
    <baseWeatherCommonalities>
      <Clear>70</Clear>
      <SnowGentle>20</SnowGentle>
      <SnowHard>25</SnowHard>
      <DryThunderstorm>2</DryThunderstorm>
      <Fog>0</Fog>
      <Rain>0</Rain>
      <RainyThunderstorm>0</RainyThunderstorm>
      <FoggyRain>0</FoggyRain>
    </baseWeatherCommonalities>
    <wildAnimals>
      <AA_Frostmite MayRequire="sarg.alphaanimals">0.35</AA_Frostmite>  <!-- frostmite - small — corpse-sweeper, the pole's undertaker, keep -->
      <AA_FrostboundBehemoth MayRequire="sarg.alphaanimals">0.126</AA_FrostboundBehemoth>  <!-- frostbound behemoth - huge — ammonia life of the Flats, keep -->
      <AA_Terramorph MayRequire="sarg.alphaanimals">0.1</AA_Terramorph>  <!-- terramorph - medium — Flats mineral chemistry, adjust-keep -->
      <AA_Slurrypede MayRequire="sarg.alphaanimals">0.02</AA_Slurrypede>  <!-- slurrypede - lab fauna — the containment facility's feeder, still running, adjust-keep -->
      <RUT_BurnerAscendant>0.03</RUT_BurnerAscendant>  <!-- the Burners, ascendant — apex of the Blue Desert's line (COMMISSION_LEDGER_CLEANUP_1, §4); mirrored from RUT_FuelSnows.xml per this file's own "full behavioural duplicate" header -->
    </wildAnimals>
    <coastalWildAnimals />
    <wildPlants>
      <AB_CrystalHorn>1.0</AB_CrystalHorn>  <!-- crystal horn -->
      <AB_FrostLeaf>0.6</AB_FrostLeaf>  <!-- frost leaf -->
      <AB_RimeNodules>0.4</AB_RimeNodules>  <!-- rime nodules -->
      <!-- SHEET_ORPHAN_CONSUMPTION_1, owner review 2026-09-20: AB_CrystalFlower moved OUT
           (kept only at poison_forest, its "elsewhere") and PoisonShrub moved IN from
           wasteland (".8 cells, propane lakes"). Both rulings landed in
           rosters/the_propane_lakes.json and reached the game only through
           BiomeFlora_Ashkarr.xml's now-retired replace operation; transplanted here by
           BIOMEFLORA_PATCH_WIPES_WILDPLANTS_1. -->
      <PoisonShrub>0.35</PoisonShrub>  <!-- poison shrub -->
    </wildPlants>
    <wildPlantRegrowDays>1</wildPlantRegrowDays>
  </BiomeDef>

</Defs>
